id: pm-ado-4x3u
title: Resolve sync conflicts with revision-bound portable field decisions
description: "Acceptance: portable base/local/remote digests with explicit per-field choices; stale Azure or local revisions refuse without changes; applied-plan replay is idempotent; omitted or conflicting choices refuse before REST writes. Typed SDK and CLI, compact receipts, docs, non-git public tracker copy plus REST 7.1 fixtures. Reuse existing three-way sync and core audited mutations and plan storage; exclude revisions-feed reconciliation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T08:25:22.374Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T11:01:24.537Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Portable base/local/remote digests with explicit per-field choices. Both local and Azure writers invalidate old plans without item changes or REST writes. Replaying an applied decision is idempotent. Missing, duplicate, conflicting or unknown choices refuse before REST writes. Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON receipts, docs and non-git public-tracker plus Azure REST 7.1 fixture acceptance."
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T08:25:42.733Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: ado sync already owns per-field base/local/remote detection and REST /rev assertions. Core SDK owns durable Plan items, complete corpus reads, history and audited mutation locks; reuse these instead of parallel storage. Sibling pm-jira transition plans and pm-linear sync do not provide Azure revision-bound conflict decisions. Revisions-feed reconciliation remains in epic scope and is excluded. Need latest SDK lease fencing for a locked callback that spans REST; evaluate 2026.10.23 before choosing the dependency floor."
  "2026-10-23T08:33:26.524Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now uses certified complete reads, authoritative SDK document reads, core Plan body persistence, staged mutation preview, and mutateItemWithHistoryContext for the locked local digest check plus REST revision assertion. SDK/dev pin and manifest/peer floor raised to 2026.10.23 because apply spans network work inside an item lease and requires #1549 fencing. REST fixtures follow Azure Work Item Tracking 7.1 hydrated revision response shape; no live credentials used. Targeted regression work covers both writers, duplicate/missing choices, replay, core Plan persistence, actual CLI TOON/JSON and PATH without git."
  "2026-10-23T08:42:26.823Z",codex-agent,"Measured public origin/main tracker copy at 1fe0a306e13417115e66de9b48ac2e50deaa25d1: 28 certified items; 224 scalar field comparisons; 28 synthetic title conflicts; 28 valid reviewed plans and 28 incomplete-choice refusals; mean JSON plan 2561 bytes; authoritative copied tracker files unchanged; zero Azure writes. Projection overlays stayed in memory, with an explicit canceled-to-Removed map. Separate disposable SDK trackers exercise real apply, CLI, lifecycle and replay behavior. Linked targeted run passed 8/8 with zero skipped; test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so the run receipt was observed and results recorded here without changing policy."
  "2026-10-23T08:43:21.112Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: independently removing the local revision guard or Azure revision/digest guard from apply makes the two-writer regression fail with Missing expected rejection (1/1 failed in each variant). Local competing writer appends a real SDK comment so field equality cannot substitute for local revision fencing. Restored implementation passes. Compatibility adjustment: pinned pm-changelog invocation needs explicit --full under current CLI full-read semantics; add that to the existing pm arguments instead of weakening complete-read validation. Local strict health saw existing stale items plus install-generated fence drift after restoring the tracked attributes; CI's normal dependency prepare step owns that installation setup; no merge-driver product work undertaken."
  "2026-10-23T08:44:20.955Z",codex-agent,"Changelog compatibility correction: pm-changelog 2026.10.16 exposes only global --pm-arg, so --full cannot be injected at the required list-local position. Use published pm-changelog 2026.10.21, whose canonical list builder already includes --full. This tooling bump is necessary for the feature's 2026.10.23 lease-fencing dependency and preserves complete-read refusal rather than bypassing it. No package implementation outside pm-ado changed."
  "2026-10-23T08:48:37.862Z",codex-agent,"Post-push inspection found a legacy-base edge: scalar resolution must not invent a partial base lacking relation agreement, or the next sync rejects it. Preserve a missing base and let existing sync establish the complete base; validate existing bases including relation shape. Added a regression that resolves a legacy item then runs real sync successfully. Targeted suite remains 8/8. PR #41 is ready for review; initial CI was queued and will be superseded by this correction."
  "2026-10-23T08:50:04.316Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local targeted verification complete in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/41. Release claim for orchestrator review without closing. Code commits: 150bb7f and adb7cd2. Local checks: 8/8 resolution cases, 3/3 shared sync/base cases, both independent guard reverts fail 1/1 as intended, source/test typechecks and 78-declaration docstring lint pass. Full release evidence is delegated to the existing CI npm/Bun jobs as instructed; exact run URL and measured counts will be verified and retained in the PR body before final handoff. Live Azure access remains unverified; documented REST 7.1 fixtures and unchanged public tracker copy supply offline acceptance."
  "2026-10-23T08:57:06.914Z",codex-agent,"Portability hardening during CI queue wait: canonical object-key hashing now uses fixed Unicode ordering instead of localeCompare, so plans do not depend on a machine's locale. Added nested Unicode key and object-insertion-order regression; restoring the locale comparator fails that test 1/1. This is a small correction to the revision coordinate itself; the existing fixture/public-copy counts and byte size are unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T09:02:04.228Z",codex-agent,"Complete the same portability correction in the existing shared canonical tag-set sorter: use fixed string ordering rather than localeCompare. Added a Unicode-tag assertion to the digest regression so per-field coordinates and canonical objects both have locale-independent ordering. This avoids valid portable plans being falsely marked stale on a different locale; it does not add a parallel projection implementation."
  "2026-10-23T09:55:31.162Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: remote branch is current and already contains origin/main, so no main merge is needed. Address both blockers on PR #41: persist a fenced, audited recovery intent before Azure PATCH and resume settlement after lease/write failures; replace raw organization/project scope in portable/saved plans with a credential-keyed opaque reference. Reuse this feature item; retain existing acceptance evidence and add real non-git tracker recovery/privacy regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs. No review-thread replies or mentions."
  "2026-10-23T10:19:20.401Z",codex-agent,"Both review blockers implemented. Apply now commits an audited target-item intent before REST (canonical plan/choice ID, local revision, Azure revision/digest, exact /rev-tested PATCH, expected next revision, reviewed values), then settles through a second fenced SDK mutation. A unique System.History marker plus expected revision and mapped values prove a prior successful PATCH; retry settles without another PATCH. Competing context, altered outcomes and unreadable intents return ado_partial_apply with the recovery coordinate and same-plan remedy. Version 2 saved plans contain only a token-keyed opaque scope reference; raw organization/project/token never enter Plan bodies or history."
  "2026-10-23T10:19:22.228Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs: removing only the durable prepare-field write fails the lease recovery regression 1/1 (intent absent before Azure); disabling applied-PATCH recognition fails real tracker-write recovery 1/1 (same plan cannot settle); replacing only opaque scope generation with raw configuration fails saved Plan/history privacy 1/1. All source restored. Targeted suite passes 18/18, zero skips; resolution.ts V8 lines/branches/functions all 100%. Real lease takeover and real filesystem permission failure after PATCH both retain intent and recover with exactly one PATCH. Privacy scans include a synthetic 84-character PAT-shaped credential and Basic encoding."
  "2026-10-23T10:21:59.068Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up verification complete locally: PM-linked targeted command passed 18/18 with zero skips; source/test typechecks and docstring lint (79 declarations) pass. Updated read-only public-copy run: 28 certified items, 224 field comparisons, 28 valid plans, 28 incomplete-choice refusals, 2576 mean JSON bytes for version 2, unchanged authoritative source fingerprints and zero Azure writes. Intent progress observer supports deterministic peer/failure interleavings without SDK mocks. Release claim for orchestrator review; keep item unclosed. The new exact-head npm/Bun CI run URL and counts will be retained in PR #41 before final handoff."
  "2026-10-23T10:29:46.827Z",codex-agent,"Tightened retry classification: read the durable intent coordinate before lease acquisition so a still-held peer lock on a post-PATCH retry returns ado_partial_apply with the original expected revision, rather than generic apply_failed. Real SDK held-lock regression passes, alongside both named failure paths (3/3 targeted). Removing only this classification makes its regression fail 1/1 with apply_failed instead of ado_partial_apply. All source restored; SDK functions remain real, not mocked."
  "2026-10-23T11:00:09.427Z",codex-agent,"Approved PR follow-up: merge current main after the toolchain dependency update, preserve the higher dependency pins and PR additions, regenerate the npm lockfile and changelog, verify installation and targeted checks, and require npm plus Bun release gates on the new head. No product changes are planned."
  "2026-10-23T11:01:23.841Z",codex-agent,"Main integration validation: chose pm-cli 2026.10.23, pm-changelog 2026.10.21 and pm-ops 2026.10.20; retained the pm-cli peer floor >=2026.10.23 and every PR dependency. npm install --package-lock-only and npm ci passed (101 audited packages, zero vulnerabilities). npm run typecheck and npm run build:test passed. Linked targeted test run via pm test pm-ado-4x3u --run --progress passed 18/18, zero failures or skips; configured evidence recording remains disabled, so results are recorded here. Product code is unchanged; the prepare launcher update is inherited unchanged from main. Final changelog generation/check and exact-head CI gates follow."
